    {
      "skill_id": "en-a1-009",
      "title": "Regular and irregular plural nouns",
      "explanation": "Most nouns add -s in the plural: book, books. Nouns ending in -s, -sh, -ch, -x or -z add -es: box, boxes; watch, watches; bus, buses. Nouns ending in a consonant plus -y change y to -ies: baby, babies (but boy, boys). Some frequent nouns are irregular and must be learned: man, men; woman, women; child, children; foot, feet; person, people. The verb after a plural subject has no -s: Two women work here.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I have two books."
        },
        {
          "en": "Two women work here."
        },
        {
          "en": "The children are happy."
        }
      ],
