    {
      "skill_id": "en-a1-010",
      "title": "Articles a, an, the and demonstratives",
      "explanation": "Use a before a consonant sound (a book) and an before a vowel sound (an apple, an hour). Use a or an when you mention something for the first time and the when it is already known: I have a book. The book is new. This and that point to one thing (near and far); these and those point to several: This book is new. Those shoes are old. The demonstrative agrees in number with the noun.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I have an apple."
        },
        {
          "en": "This book is new."
        },
        {
          "en": "Those shoes are old."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["CAM-A1-YLE"],
