      "skill_id": "en-a1-013",
      "title": "Subject and object pronouns",
      "explanation": "Subject pronouns come before the verb: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Object pronouns come after the verb or a preposition: me, you, him, her, it, us, them. She sees me. I help them. This is for her. After a verb or preposition never use the subject form: not She sees I. Demonstratives such as this and that can also stand alone: This is for her.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "She sees me."
        },
        {
          "en": "I help them."
        },
        {
          "en": "This is for her."
        }
